WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Your own grooves
Record an instrument into the style's groove, and Polly keeps an edited copy.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:09.280
1. Pick an instrument
Press HOME for the Home page. Turn KNOB 4 (Prog) down, past P1, to "follow". The band follows your chords, not the song.

3
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:16.286
1. Pick an instrument
Hold HOME and press black key 2 for Groove A.

4
00:00:16.286 --> 00:00:24.657
1. Pick an instrument
Press PLAY. Press SEQ for the Band page, and turn ALGORITHM to C2. Its row is empty.

5
00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:32.350
2. Record
Press REC. Polly makes an edited copy and marks it Groove A (edited). Play from the next bar.

6
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:38.972
2. Record
The groove keeps looping, so you can keep adding notes. Press REC again to stop.

7
00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:45.452
3. Make it longer
Turn SELECT to the Groove length page. Turn KNOB 1 (Bars) to 4.

8
00:00:45.452 --> 00:00:51.912
4. Change the style
Press HOME and turn KNOB 1 (Style) to Funk. Polly asks if you want to keep Groove A.

9
00:00:51.912 --> 00:00:57.542
4. Change the style
Press SEL to keep it. Your Groove A plays with Funk's band.

10
00:00:57.542 --> 00:01:02.082
5. Give the groove back
Press PLAY to stop. Press SEQ, then SEL for the list.

11
00:01:02.082 --> 00:01:09.312
5. Give the groove back
Turn SELECT to BACK TO STYLE and press SEL. Your copy stays in Memory.

12
00:01:09.312 --> 00:01:13.400
Next: 107
Fixing notes.
